{"type":"standard","title":"Erromanga language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Erromanga language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q426254","titles":{"canonical":"Erromanga_language","normalized":"Erromanga language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Erromanga language</span></span>"},"pageid":16639574,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Erromangomap.png/330px-Erromangomap.png","width":330,"height":305},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/04/Erromangomap.png","width":545,"height":504},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1341929006","tid":"0aa38636-18ed-11f1-83d8-cf4b4aa3d6d7","timestamp":"2026-03-05T23:42:59Z","description":"Austronesian language spoken in Vanuatu","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erromanga_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erromanga_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erromanga_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Erromanga_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erromanga_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Erromanga_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erromanga_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Erromanga_language"}},"extract":"Erromangan, or Sie (Sye), is the primary language spoken on the island Erromango in the Tafea region of the Vanuatu islands. The other Erromanga languages are either moribund or extinct. Although the island is quite large (887 km2), the total number of speakers of Erromango is estimated at 1900.","extract_html":"<p><b>Erromangan</b>, or <b>Sie</b> (Sye), is the primary language spoken on the island Erromango in the Tafea region of the Vanuatu islands. The other Erromanga languages are either moribund or extinct. Although the island is quite large (887 km<sup>2</sup>), the total number of speakers of Erromango is estimated at 1900.</p>"}